course: dictionary
lesson: 11869
title: A word with two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word boon has two. Most of the time it means something very helpful that makes life better. «The new library is a boon to the village.» The library makes life better for everyone there, so it is a boon.
explain: In old stories, boon means a favour or a request. «The brave knight knelt and asked the king for a boon.» The knight is asking the king for a special favour. You will find this meaning mostly in old tales, not in everyday talk.
explain: To choose the right meaning, use the clues around the word. Ask: is the sentence about something helpful, or about someone asking for a favour? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Boon is a noun. You can write a boon or boons.
fact: Boon means something very helpful that makes life better.
fact: In old stories, a boon is a favour or a request that someone asks for.
fact: «A boon companion» is an old phrase for a close friend.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so always check the context.
exercise: «Rain after the long dry summer was a boon to the farmers.» What does boon mean here? | * Something very helpful that makes life better | A cold wind | A loud noise | A sad story
exercise: In an old tale, the hero says, «Please grant me one boon, my king.» What is a boon in this story? | A large stone castle | * A favour or request | A hot meal | A long journey
exercise: «The new bus route is a boon to people who work far away.» Is a boon good news or bad news here? | Neither, it is a colour | * Good, it helps people | Bad, it is very loud | Bad, it stops people getting to work
test: Which word could replace boon in «The warm coat was a boon on the cold walk»? | * A great help | A burden | A short trip | A puzzle
test: In an old story, what might a boon be? | A painted door | * A favour asked of a king | A letter from a friend | A storm at sea
exam: Which is the right meaning of boon in «The knight asked the king for one boon»? | A very helpful thing | A long road | * A favour or request | A sad song
